From fd00d114f2eedab18721f96db020223537c6f73b Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Carlos Cueto <crcueto25@gmail.com>
Date: Thu, 15 Oct 2026 07:43:21 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] dude-0: order DuDe vertices and BPCs by creation, not by
 address

PATCH(dude-0). DuDe ordered by pointer value where the order reaches its
result: the four set<ply_vertex *> of c_dude (combineMinimumPnts,
collectPMs, the outer and the total feature points) and the tie break of
reorganize_kids_f (list<pair<int, c_BPC *>>::sort). That order was
stable only while DuDe leaked (the heap grew with the creation order);
with the leak fixes D1 to D4f a second decomposition in the same process
gave other cuts under some heap layouts. Each ply_vertex and c_BPC now
gets a creation number (dude_seq: one process-wide std::atomic<uint64_t>,
relaxed fetch_add; a copy gets a new number, an assignment keeps the
target's), and those containers order by it (null first). Searched and
left as is (order does not reach the result): the vertex lookup maps,
SE2d::ply2MouthMap and the sets of SE2d::destroy(), the cutset angle
sort (by vector position), the approximation heap (by distance), the
graph sorts (by id). DudeReference matches its golden, and a second pass
gives the same result, under six glibc malloc layouts and in ctest.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
